  "description": "Proposed part single and part double storey side and rear extensions to allow for the conversion of the existing property from Use Class C4 (HMO) to Use Class C2 (Care Home) - 18 Bedrooms, with internal and external communal areas, and other spaces required to serve the care home, and associated landscaping, refuse and recycle storage, cycle storage and car parking provisions.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in an overly large and prominent addition to the streetscene, within the heart of the Ruislip Village Conservation Area which would neither preserve or enhance the existing building and the wider conservation area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies BE1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part One Strategic Policies (2012), and DMHB1, DMHB 11, DMHB 12, and DMHD 1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two: Development Management Policies (2020), which aim to ensure that new development is in keeping with the existing build environment, and does not give rise to adverse impacts on the character and appearance of conservation areas or designated heritage assets.",
    "The proposal, by way of the overly large and prominent proposed extension to the building, results in an increased sense of enclosure and loss of outlook to the private amenity space and habitable room windows at no. 11 Sharps Lane. It is therefore considered that the proposal is contrary to Policy Policy DMHB 11 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part 2 Development Management Policies (2020).",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted to adequately determine that the loss of habitat in line with statutory Biodiversity Net Gain could not be mitigated on site. As such, the proposed development does not accord with the Biodiversity net Gain Hierarchy set out in Articles 37A and 37D of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy G6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DMEI 7 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part 2 Development Management Policies (2020), which seek to conserve and enhance biodiversity and secure measurable net gains."
  ],
